  (text "MAIN MCU: STM32U5G9NJH6Q, TFBGA-216 13x13 mm, 0.8 mm pitch. Pin functions are taken from the KiCad library's\nalternate-function data. Every ball not listed in PINMAP is left unconnected (spare GPIO).\n\nMUST BE CONFIRMED AGAINST THE DATASHEET AND AN5373 BEFORE REVIEW (st.com was not reachable):\n 1. SMPS network: L1 value and the capacitor on each VDD11 ball (C20-C22).\n 2. VDD11USB: whether it is tied to VDD11 (R20 fitted) or only decoupled (R20 not fitted).\n 3. DSI unused: required connection of VDDDSI, VDD11DSI/VCAPDSI and the DSI balls.\n 4. VBAT: tied to +3V3 through R21 for now; becomes the coin-cell backup rail if tamper-in-storage is adopted.\n 5. HSE 16 MHz (as on ST's dev kit) is assumed valid for the USB HS PHY; crystal load capacitors C30-C33 are placeholders.\n 6. Decoupling count and values (C10-C19, C23-C29) are defaults.\nNets ending in another sheet that is not drawn yet (display, touch, secure element, BLE, NFC, charger) are single-ended for now."
    (at 25 20 0)
    (effects
      (font
